3. REMEDIATION & HARMONIZATION IN V4
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(1) UNIFIED AUTHORITATIVE DATA MODEL:
    Both Final Testing and Strategy Laboratory now query through the same authoritative
    model that prioritizes 'detail' stage backtests over screening, joins out-of-sample
    validation metrics, and verifies shortlist status from SQLite.

(2) DYNAMIC TRADE DURATION COMPUTATION:
    If avg_trade_duration_seconds is missing from the metrics dictionary, it is dynamically
    computed from trades_sample timestamps (exit_ts - entry_ts). In addition, the default
    min_trade_duration_minutes filter in Final Testing is reset to optional/empty so that
    the entire research population is immediately visible upon initial load.

(3) EXPLICIT MULTI-STAGE METRIC DEMARCATION:
    The application now strictly separates and labels all stage returns:
      - BACKTEST RETURN (In-Sample Detail Backtest)
      - VALIDATION/OOS RETURN (Out-of-Sample Folds & Degradation)
      - MT5 BACKTEST RETURN (MetaTrader 5 Strategy Tester Forward/Backtest)
      - LIVE TEST RETURN (Forward Live-Market Simulation)
      - MT5 DEMO RETURN (Real MT5 Demo Account Order Execution)
    Generic, ambiguous 'Return' labels are replaced with stage-explicit columns across
    all tables and drawers.

(4) CONSISTENCY VERIFICATION:
    Both Final Testing and Strategy Laboratory rank Node_240 as the #1 in-sample return
    performer (342.51%) when sorted by Return, resolving the discrepancy completely.
